\caption{Violation rates (\%) by model and type under ambiguous conditions ($n = 2{,}997$). Authorization scope varies 52\,pp across models ($\kappa = 0.385$), reflecting differential safety training; incompleteness remains uniformly high (46--62\%). C4 interaction is authorization-scope-specific (\S\ref{sec:c4}).}
\label{fig:heatmap}
\end{figure}

\label{sec:c4}C4 (model$\times$type interaction) is exploratory. The interaction is driven entirely by authorization scope (Claude 12\% vs.\ GPT-5.4/DeepSeek $>$60\%; Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap}); excluding it, the interaction vanishes ($p = 0.97$; Appendix~\ref{app:c4_sans_auth}). Cross-judge validation confirms model rankings (Fleiss' $\kappa = 0.717$; Appendix~\ref{app:cross_judge}).

